IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `ccc-core`

-- ccc10-kidnapping.l4 -- sections 279 to 286 of the Criminal Code (Canada), R.S.C., 1985, c. C-46: kidnapping, trafficking in persons, hostage taking,
-- abduction of a young person, and the defences and the "no defence" rule that go with the abduction offences. Layer 1 (the law, objectively).
-- Source: a plain-text rendering, made by a converter script, of the Justice Laws Website consolidation (current to 2026-09-30).
-- It is not the official text, and nothing here is claimed verified against the official text.
-- How a result reads: JUST TRUE (every element holds, or the defence is made out); JUST FALSE (the text says no in its own words, quoted in the branch's
-- comment); NOTHING (not covered: an element is missing, the text is silent or limits a prohibition in its own wording, or the answer points outside the text).
-- A caller never turns NOTHING into FALSE. Seams: `s 2.1 ...`, `s 2 ...` are the keel's answers; `s 787(1) ...` is ccc29's; all are inputs of the answering function's type.
-- Periods the core lacks (four, seven years) are written inline: `Length of time` OF 4, 0, 0, FALSE (NEEDS-CORE.md item 3).

§ `s 279 -- Kidnapping`

-- 279(1): the offence. "kidnaps" is not defined in the text: a plain fact.
-- src:5658 | 279 (1) Every person commits an offence who kidnaps a person with intent
-- src:5659 | (a) to cause the person to be confined or imprisoned against the person’s will;
-- src:5660 | (b) to cause the person to be unlawfully sent or transported out of Canada against the person’s will; or
-- src:5661 | (c) to hold the person for ransom or to service against the person’s will.
@ref s 279(1) (src:5658-5661)
GIVEN `the person kidnaps a person` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person kidnaps with intent to cause the person to be confined or imprisoned against the person’s will` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person kidnaps with intent to cause the person to be unlawfully sent or transported out of Canada against the person’s will` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person kidnaps with intent to hold the person for ransom or to service against the person’s will` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 279(1) the person commits the offence of kidnapping` MEANS
    IF `the person kidnaps a person`
       AND (   `the person kidnaps with intent to cause the person to be confined or imprisoned against the person’s will`
            OR `the person kidnaps with intent to cause the person to be unlawfully sent or transported out of Canada against the person’s will`
            OR `the person kidnaps with intent to hold the person for ransom or to service against the person’s will`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Every person commits an offence who kidnaps a person with intent"

-- 279(1.1): the punishment. Paragraphs (a), (a.1) and (a.2) can all apply to one set of facts (a firearm and a victim under 16): taken as cumulative,
-- the greatest minimum applies (fork F20). A NOTHING in any defined-term input gives NOTHING (fork F21).
-- src:5662 | Punishment
-- src:5663 | (1.1) Every person who commits an offence under subsection (1) is guilty of an indictable offence and liable
-- src:5664 | (a) if a restricted firearm or prohibited firearm is used in the commission of the offence or if any firearm is used in the commission of the offence and the offence is committed for the benefit of, at the direction of, or in association with, a criminal organization, to imprisonment for life and to a minimum punishment of imprisonment for a term of
-- src:5665 | (i) in the case of a first offence, five years, and
-- src:5666 | (ii) in the case of a second or subsequent offence, seven years;
-- src:5667 | (a.1) in any other case where a firearm is used in the commission of the offence, to imprisonment for life and to a minimum punishment of imprisonment for a term of four years;
-- src:5668 | (a.2) if the person referred to in paragraph (1)(a), (b) or (c) is under 16 years of age, to imprisonment for life and, unless the person who commits the offence is a parent, guardian or person having the lawful care or charge of the person referred to in that paragraph, to a minimum punishment of imprisonment for a term of five years; and
-- src:5669 | (b) in any other case, to imprisonment for life.
@ref s 279(1.1) (src:5662-5669)
GIVEN `s 2.1 restricted firearm: a restricted firearm is used in the commission of the offence` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `s 2.1 prohibited firearm: a prohibited firearm is used in the commission of the offence` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `s 2 firearm: a firearm is used in the commission of the offence` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `s 2 criminal organization: the offence is committed for the benefit of, at the direction of, or in association with, a criminal organization` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the answer of s 279(1.2) as to a second or subsequent offence` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the person referred to in paragraph (1)(a), (b) or (c) is under 16 years of age` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person who commits the offence is a parent, guardian or person having the lawful care or charge of the person referred to in that paragraph` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE Punishment
`s 279(1.1) the punishment` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF    (`s 2.1 restricted firearm: a restricted firearm is used in the commission of the offence` EQUALS NOTHING)
           OR (`s 2.1 prohibited firearm: a prohibited firearm is used in the commission of the offence` EQUALS NOTHING)
           OR (`s 2 firearm: a firearm is used in the commission of the offence` EQUALS NOTHING)
           OR (`s 2 criminal organization: the offence is committed for the benefit of, at the direction of, or in association with, a criminal organization` EQUALS NOTHING)
        THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): which firearm, and whether a criminal organization is involved, are for s 2, s 2.1 and s 84(1) and s 467.1(1), and are not determined
        IF `paragraph (a) applies` AND (`the answer of s 279(1.2) as to a second or subsequent offence` EQUALS NOTHING)
        THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether this is a second or subsequent offence is for s 279(1.2) and is not determined
        OTHERWISE JUST (Punishment OF `by indictment`, `imprisonment for life`, `the minimum imprisonment`, `no fine is stated`, `no fine is stated`)
    WHERE
        `paragraph (a) applies` MEANS
                (`s 2.1 restricted firearm: a restricted firearm is used in the commission of the offence` EQUALS JUST TRUE)
             OR (`s 2.1 prohibited firearm: a prohibited firearm is used in the commission of the offence` EQUALS JUST TRUE)
             OR ((`s 2 firearm: a firearm is used in the commission of the offence` EQUALS JUST TRUE) AND (`s 2 criminal organization: the offence is committed for the benefit of, at the direction of, or in association with, a criminal organization` EQUALS JUST TRUE))
        `paragraph (a.1) applies` MEANS (`s 2 firearm: a firearm is used in the commission of the offence` EQUALS JUST TRUE) AND (NOT `paragraph (a) applies`)
        `paragraph (a.2) applies` MEANS `the person referred to in paragraph (1)(a), (b) or (c) is under 16 years of age`
        -- ruler: the minimum in years under (a) [5 first, 7 second or subsequent], (a.1) [4], (a.2) [5 unless a parent, guardian or person having lawful care or charge]
        `minimum under (a)` MEANS IF `paragraph (a) applies` THEN (IF `the answer of s 279(1.2) as to a second or subsequent offence` EQUALS JUST TRUE THEN 7 ELSE 5) ELSE 0
        `minimum under (a.1)` MEANS IF `paragraph (a.1) applies` THEN 4 ELSE 0
        `minimum under (a.2)` MEANS IF `paragraph (a.2) applies` AND (NOT `the person who commits the offence is a parent, guardian or person having the lawful care or charge of the person referred to in that paragraph`) THEN 5 ELSE 0
        `the minimum in years` MEANS
            BRANCH
                IF `minimum under (a)` AT LEAST `minimum under (a.1)` AND `minimum under (a)` AT LEAST `minimum under (a.2)` THEN `minimum under (a)`
                IF `minimum under (a.1)` AT LEAST `minimum under (a.2)` THEN `minimum under (a.1)`
                OTHERWISE `minimum under (a.2)`
        `the minimum imprisonment` MEANS
            IF `the minimum in years` EQUALS 0 THEN `no imprisonment is stated` ELSE `imprisonment for a term of` (`Length of time` OF `the minimum in years`, 0, 0, FALSE)

@ref s 279(1.1) (src:5662-5663)
`s 279(1.1) the class of the offence` MEANS `an indictable offence`

-- 279(1.2): which earlier convictions count. A conviction is an "earlier offence" if it is of a listed offence and ten years have not elapsed.
-- src:5670 | Subsequent offences
-- src:5671 | (1.2) In determining, for the purpose of paragraph (1.1)(a), whether a convicted person has committed a second or subsequent offence, if the person was earlier convicted of any of the following offences, that offence is to be considered as an earlier offence:
-- src:5672 | (a) an offence under subsection (1);
-- src:5673 | (b) an offence under subsection 85(1) or (2) or section 244 or 244.2; or
-- src:5674 | (c) an offence under section 220, 236, 239, 272, 273, 279.1, 344 or 346 if a firearm was used in the commission of the offence.
-- src:5675 | However, an earlier offence shall not be taken into account if 10 years have elapsed between the day on which the person was convicted of the earlier offence and the day on which the person was convicted of the offence for which sentence is being imposed, not taking into account any time in custody.
@ref s 279(1.2) (src:5670-5675)
DECLARE `s 279(1.2) earlier conviction` HAS
    `the offence of which the person was convicted`                     IS A `Provision of the Code`
    `a firearm was used in the commission of that offence`              IS A BOOLEAN
    `the day on which the person was convicted of that offence`         IS A DATE
    `the days in custody between the two convictions`                   IS A NUMBER

@ref s 279(1.2) (src:5670-5675)
GIVEN conviction IS A `s 279(1.2) earlier conviction`
      `the day on which the person was convicted of the offence for which sentence is being imposed` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 279(1.2) the conviction is to be considered as an earlier offence` MEANS
    IF NOT `the conviction is of an offence the subsection lists`
    THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "if the person was earlier convicted of any of the following offences, that offence is to be considered as an earlier offence"
    ELSE IF `ten years have elapsed`
         THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "an earlier offence shall not be taken into account if 10 years have elapsed between the day on which the person was convicted of the earlier offence and the day on which the person was convicted of the offence for which sentence is being imposed, not taking into account any time in custody"
         ELSE JUST TRUE
    WHERE
        sec MEANS conviction's `the offence of which the person was convicted`'s `section`
        sub MEANS conviction's `the offence of which the person was convicted`'s `subsection`
        `the conviction is of an offence the subsection lists` MEANS
                (sec EQUALS 279 AND sub EQUALS "(1)")
             OR (sec EQUALS 85 AND (sub EQUALS "(1)" OR sub EQUALS "(2)"))
             OR sec EQUALS 244 OR sec EQUALS 244.2
             OR (   (sec EQUALS 220 OR sec EQUALS 236 OR sec EQUALS 239 OR sec EQUALS 272 OR sec EQUALS 273 OR sec EQUALS 279.1 OR sec EQUALS 344 OR sec EQUALS 346)
                AND conviction's `a firearm was used in the commission of that offence`)
        `the anniversary ten years after the earlier conviction` MEANS
            Date (DATE_DAY (conviction's `the day on which the person was convicted of that offence`)) (DATE_MONTH (conviction's `the day on which the person was convicted of that offence`)) ((DATE_YEAR (conviction's `the day on which the person was convicted of that offence`)) PLUS 10)
        -- ten years have elapsed when the time between the two convictions, less the days in custody, reaches the tenth anniversary
        `ten years have elapsed` MEANS
            ((DATE_SERIAL `the day on which the person was convicted of the offence for which sentence is being imposed`) MINUS conviction's `the days in custody between the two convictions`) AT LEAST (DATE_SERIAL `the anniversary ten years after the earlier conviction`)

-- 279(1.3): only the sequence of convictions counts, never the sequence of commission.
-- src:5678 | Sequence of convictions only
-- src:5679 | (1.3) For the purposes of subsection (1.2), the only question to be considered is the sequence of convictions and no consideration shall be given to the sequence of commission of offences or whether any offence occurred before or after any conviction.
@ref s 279(1.3) (src:5678-5679)
GIVEN `the day on which the person was convicted of the earlier offence` IS A DATE
      `the day on which the person was convicted of the offence for which sentence is being imposed` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 279(1.3) the conviction is earlier in the sequence of convictions` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF (DATE_SERIAL `the day on which the person was convicted of the earlier offence`) LESS THAN (DATE_SERIAL `the day on which the person was convicted of the offence for which sentence is being imposed`) THEN JUST TRUE
        IF (DATE_SERIAL `the day on which the person was convicted of the earlier offence`) GREATER THAN (DATE_SERIAL `the day on which the person was convicted of the offence for which sentence is being imposed`) THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the only question to be considered is the sequence of convictions" (a conviction that follows in the sequence is not an earlier one)
        OTHERWISE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the text does not say how two convictions on the same day are sequenced

-- "second or subsequent" from the list of earlier convictions, by (1.2) and (1.3). An empty list, or every conviction barred, is a first offence.
@ref s 279(1.2) and (1.3) (src:5678-5679)
GIVEN `the earlier convictions` IS A LIST OF `s 279(1.2) earlier conviction`
      `the day on which the person was convicted of the offence for which sentence is being imposed` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 279(1.2) the person has committed a second or subsequent offence` MEANS
    IF any (GIVEN c IS A `s 279(1.2) earlier conviction` YIELD (`the conviction counts` c) EQUALS JUST TRUE) `the earlier convictions`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE IF any (GIVEN c IS A `s 279(1.2) earlier conviction` YIELD (`the conviction counts` c) EQUALS NOTHING) `the earlier convictions`
         THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): an earlier conviction of an offence the subsection does not list, or on the same day, is not said to count or not to count
         ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "in the case of a first offence" (no earlier conviction counts: none, or each is barred by ten years)
    WHERE
        `the conviction counts` c MEANS
            BRANCH
                IF (`s 279(1.3) the conviction is earlier in the sequence of convictions` (c's `the day on which the person was convicted of that offence`) `the day on which the person was convicted of the offence for which sentence is being imposed`) EQUALS JUST FALSE THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the only question to be considered is the sequence of convictions"
                IF (`s 279(1.3) the conviction is earlier in the sequence of convictions` (c's `the day on which the person was convicted of that offence`) `the day on which the person was convicted of the offence for which sentence is being imposed`) EQUALS NOTHING THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): two convictions on one day
                OTHERWISE `s 279(1.2) the conviction is to be considered as an earlier offence` c `the day on which the person was convicted of the offence for which sentence is being imposed`

-- src:5677 | (1.21) In imposing a sentence under paragraph (1.1)(a.2), the court shall take into account the age and vulnerability of the victim.
@ref s 279(1.21) (src:5677)
GIVEN `the sentence is imposed under paragraph (1.1)(a.2)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 279(1.21) the court shall take into account the age and vulnerability of the victim` MEANS
    IF `the sentence is imposed under paragraph (1.1)(a.2)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "In imposing a sentence under paragraph (1.1)(a.2)"

DECLARE `s 279(1.21) the act of the court` IS ONE OF `s 279(1.21) take into account the age and vulnerability of the victim`

@ref s 279(1.21) (src:5677)
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 279(1.21) the act of the court`
`s 279(1.21) the duty of the court` MEANS
    PARTY `the court`
    MUST `s 279(1.21) take into account the age and vulnerability of the victim`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `the court` BECAUSE "the age and vulnerability of the victim were not taken into account in imposing a sentence under paragraph 279(1.1)(a.2)"

-- 279(2): forcible confinement, hybrid: ten years on indictment; the summary penalty is s 787(1) (a seam).
-- src:5680 | Forcible confinement
-- src:5681 | (2) Every one who, without lawful authority, confines, imprisons or forcibly seizes another person is guilty of
-- src:5682 | (a) an indictable offence and liable to imprisonment for a term not exceeding ten years; or
-- src:5683 | (b) an offence punishable on summary conviction.
@ref s 279(2) (src:5680-5683)
GIVEN `the person confines, imprisons or forcibly seizes another person` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person does so without lawful authority` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 279(2) the person is guilty of the offence of forcible confinement` MEANS
    IF `the person confines, imprisons or forcibly seizes another person` AND `the person does so without lawful authority`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Every one who, without lawful authority, confines, imprisons or forcibly seizes another person"

@ref s 279(2) (src:5680-5683)
`s 279(2) the class of the offence` MEANS `an offence that the section makes both indictable and punishable on summary conviction`

@ref s 279(2) (src:5682-5683)
GIVEN mode IS A `Mode of proceeding`
      `s 787(1) the general penalty for an offence punishable on summary conviction` IS A Punishment
GIVETH A Punishment
`s 279(2) the punishment` MEANS
    CONSIDER mode
    WHEN `by indictment` THEN Punishment OF `by indictment`, (`imprisonment for a term of` `ten years`), `no imprisonment is stated`, `no fine is stated`, `no fine is stated`
    WHEN `on summary conviction` THEN `s 787(1) the general penalty for an offence punishable on summary conviction`

-- src:5684 | (3) [Repealed, 2018, c. 29, s. 26]
@ref s 279(3) (src:5684)
`s 279(3) as the text shows it` MEANS "[Repealed, 2018, c. 29, s. 26]"


§ `s 279.01 -- Trafficking in persons`

-- src:5686 | 279.01 (1) Every person who recruits, transports, transfers, receives, holds, conceals or harbours a person, or exercises control, direction or influence over the movements of a person, for the purpose of exploiting them or facilitating their exploitation is guilty of an indictable offence and liable
-- src:5687 | (a) to imprisonment for life and to a minimum punishment of imprisonment for a term of five years if they kidnap, commit an aggravated assault or aggravated sexual assault against, or cause death to, the victim during the commission of the offence; or
-- src:5688 | (b) to imprisonment for a term of not more than 14 years and to a minimum punishment of imprisonment for a term of four years in any other case.
@ref s 279.01(1) (src:5686-5688)
GIVEN `the person recruits, transports, transfers, receives, holds, conceals or harbours a person, or exercises control, direction or influence over the movements of a person` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person does so for the purpose of exploiting them or facilitating their exploitation` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 279.01(1) the person is guilty of the offence of trafficking in persons` MEANS
    IF `the person recruits, transports, transfers, receives, holds, conceals or harbours a person, or exercises control, direction or influence over the movements of a person` AND `the person does so for the purpose of exploiting them or facilitating their exploitation`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "for the purpose of exploiting them or facilitating their exploitation"

@ref s 279.01(1) (src:5686-5688)
`s 279.01(1) the class of the offence` MEANS `an indictable offence`

@ref s 279.01(1) (src:5687-5688)
GIVEN `during the commission of the offence they kidnap, commit an aggravated assault or aggravated sexual assault against, or cause death to, the victim` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A Punishment
`s 279.01(1) the punishment` MEANS
    IF `during the commission of the offence they kidnap, commit an aggravated assault or aggravated sexual assault against, or cause death to, the victim`
    THEN Punishment OF `by indictment`, `imprisonment for life`, (`imprisonment for a term of` `five years`), `no fine is stated`, `no fine is stated`
    ELSE Punishment OF `by indictment`, (`imprisonment for a term of` `fourteen years`), (`imprisonment for a term of` (`Length of time` OF 4, 0, 0, FALSE)), `no fine is stated`, `no fine is stated`

-- 279.01(2): "No consent ... is valid": a flat negative, for a charge under (1).
-- src:5689 | Consent
-- src:5690 | (2) No consent to the activity that forms the subject-matter of a charge under subsection (1) is valid.
@ref s 279.01(2) (src:5689-5690)
