    IF `the charge is under subsection 279.01(1)`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "No consent to the activity that forms the subject-matter of a charge under subsection (1) is valid"
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "a charge under subsection (1)"

-- 279.01(3): the presumption. In the absence of evidence to the contrary the evidence is proof; with contrary evidence the text is silent (fork F22).
-- src:5691 | Presumption
-- src:5692 | (3) For the purposes of subsections (1) and 279.011(1), evidence that a person who is not exploited lives with or is habitually in the company of a person who is exploited is, in the absence of evidence to the contrary, proof that the person exercises control, direction or influence over the movements of that person for the purpose of exploiting them or facilitating their exploitation.
@ref s 279.01(3) (src:5691-5692)
GIVEN `the person is not exploited` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person lives with or is habitually in the company of a person who is exploited` IS A BOOLEAN
      `there is evidence to the contrary` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 279.01(3) the evidence is proof that the person exercises control, direction or influence over the movements of that person for the purpose of exploiting them` MEANS
    IF `the person is not exploited` AND `the person lives with or is habitually in the company of a person who is exploited` AND (NOT `there is evidence to the contrary`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "in the absence of evidence to the contrary" (evidence to the contrary, or the facts of the presumption absent)

