§ `s 279.02 -- Material benefit -- trafficking`

-- src:5700 | 279.02 (1) Every person who receives a financial or other material benefit, knowing that it is obtained by or derived directly or indirectly from the commission of an offence under subsection 279.01(1), is guilty of
-- src:5701 | (a) an indictable offence and liable to imprisonment for a term of not more than 10 years; or
-- src:5702 | (b) an offence punishable on summary conviction.
@ref s 279.02(1) (src:5700-5702)
GIVEN `the person receives a financial or other material benefit` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person knows that it is obtained by or derived directly or indirectly from the commission of an offence under subsection 279.01(1)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 279.02(1) the person is guilty of the offence of receiving a material benefit from trafficking` MEANS
    IF `the person receives a financial or other material benefit` AND `the person knows that it is obtained by or derived directly or indirectly from the commission of an offence under subsection 279.01(1)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "knowing that it is obtained by or derived directly or indirectly from the commission of an offence under subsection 279.01(1)"

@ref s 279.02(1) (src:5700-5702)
`s 279.02(1) the class of the offence` MEANS `an offence that the section makes both indictable and punishable on summary conviction`

@ref s 279.02(1) (src:5701-5702)
GIVEN mode IS A `Mode of proceeding`
      `s 787(1) the general penalty for an offence punishable on summary conviction` IS A Punishment
GIVETH A Punishment
`s 279.02(1) the punishment` MEANS
    CONSIDER mode
    WHEN `by indictment` THEN Punishment OF `by indictment`, (`imprisonment for a term of` `ten years`), `no imprisonment is stated`, `no fine is stated`, `no fine is stated`
    WHEN `on summary conviction` THEN `s 787(1) the general penalty for an offence punishable on summary conviction`

-- src:5703 | Material benefit — trafficking of person under 18 years
-- src:5704 | (2) Everyone who receives a financial or other material benefit, knowing that it is obtained by or derived directly or indirectly from the commission of an offence under subsection 279.011(1), is guilty of an indictable offence and liable to imprisonment for a term of not more than 14 years and to a minimum punishment of imprisonment for a term of two years.
@ref s 279.02(2) (src:5703-5704)
GIVEN `the person receives a financial or other material benefit` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person knows that it is obtained by or derived directly or indirectly from the commission of an offence under subsection 279.011(1)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 279.02(2) the person is guilty of the offence of receiving a material benefit from trafficking of a person under 18 years` MEANS
    IF `the person receives a financial or other material benefit` AND `the person knows that it is obtained by or derived directly or indirectly from the commission of an offence under subsection 279.011(1)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "knowing that it is obtained by or derived directly or indirectly from the commission of an offence under subsection 279.011(1)"

@ref s 279.02(2) (src:5703-5704)
`s 279.02(2) the class of the offence` MEANS `an indictable offence`

@ref s 279.02(2) (src:5703-5704)
`s 279.02(2) the punishment` MEANS Punishment OF `by indictment`, (`imprisonment for a term of` `fourteen years`), (`imprisonment for a term of` `two years`), `no fine is stated`, `no fine is stated`

§ `s 279.03 -- Withholding or destroying documents -- trafficking`

-- src:5706 | 279.03 (1) Every person who, for the purpose of committing or facilitating an offence under subsection 279.01(1), conceals, removes, withholds or destroys any travel document that belongs to another person or any document that establishes or purports to establish another person’s identity or immigration status — whether or not the document is of Canadian origin or is authentic — is guilty of
-- src:5707 | (a) an indictable offence and liable to imprisonment for a term of not more than five years; or
-- src:5708 | (b) an offence punishable on summary conviction.
@ref s 279.03(1) (src:5706-5708)
GIVEN `the person conceals, removes, withholds or destroys a travel document that belongs to another person or a document that establishes or purports to establish another person’s identity or immigration status` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person does so for the purpose of committing or facilitating an offence under subsection 279.01(1)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 279.03(1) the person is guilty of the offence of withholding or destroying documents` MEANS
    IF `the person conceals, removes, withholds or destroys a travel document that belongs to another person or a document that establishes or purports to establish another person’s identity or immigration status` AND `the person does so for the purpose of committing or facilitating an offence under subsection 279.01(1)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "for the purpose of committing or facilitating an offence under subsection 279.01(1)"

@ref s 279.03(1) (src:5706-5708)
`s 279.03(1) the class of the offence` MEANS `an offence that the section makes both indictable and punishable on summary conviction`

@ref s 279.03(1) (src:5707-5708)
GIVEN mode IS A `Mode of proceeding`
      `s 787(1) the general penalty for an offence punishable on summary conviction` IS A Punishment
GIVETH A Punishment
`s 279.03(1) the punishment` MEANS
    CONSIDER mode
    WHEN `by indictment` THEN Punishment OF `by indictment`, (`imprisonment for a term of` `five years`), `no imprisonment is stated`, `no fine is stated`, `no fine is stated`
    WHEN `on summary conviction` THEN `s 787(1) the general penalty for an offence punishable on summary conviction`

-- src:5709 | Withholding or destroying documents — trafficking of person under 18 years
-- src:5710 | (2) Everyone who, for the purpose of committing or facilitating an offence under subsection 279.011(1), conceals, removes, withholds or destroys any travel document that belongs to another person or any document that establishes or purports to establish another person’s identity or immigration status — whether or not the document is of Canadian origin or is authentic — is guilty of an indictable offence and liable to imprisonment for a term of not more than 10 years and to a minimum punishment of imprisonment for a term of one year.
@ref s 279.03(2) (src:5709-5710)
GIVEN `the person conceals, removes, withholds or destroys a travel document that belongs to another person or a document that establishes or purports to establish another person’s identity or immigration status` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person does so for the purpose of committing or facilitating an offence under subsection 279.011(1)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 279.03(2) the person is guilty of the offence of withholding or destroying documents -- trafficking of a person under 18 years` MEANS
    IF `the person conceals, removes, withholds or destroys a travel document that belongs to another person or a document that establishes or purports to establish another person’s identity or immigration status` AND `the person does so for the purpose of committing or facilitating an offence under subsection 279.011(1)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "for the purpose of committing or facilitating an offence under subsection 279.011(1)"

@ref s 279.03(2) (src:5709-5710)
`s 279.03(2) the class of the offence` MEANS `an indictable offence`

@ref s 279.03(2) (src:5709-5710)
`s 279.03(2) the punishment` MEANS Punishment OF `by indictment`, (`imprisonment for a term of` `ten years`), (`imprisonment for a term of` (`Length of time` OF 1, 0, 0, FALSE)), `no fine is stated`, `no fine is stated`

§ `s 279.04 -- Exploitation`

-- 279.04(1): "exploits ... if" the person causes labour or a service by conduct that could reasonably be expected to cause the belief. A failed "if" is JUST FALSE within (1); (3) is a second sufficient route (fork F23).
-- src:5712 | 279.04 (1) For the purposes of sections 279.01 to 279.03, a person exploits another person if they cause them to provide, or offer to provide, labour or a service by engaging in conduct that, in all the circumstances, could reasonably be expected to cause the other person to believe that their safety or the safety of a person known to them would be threatened if they failed to provide, or offer to provide, the labour or service.
@ref s 279.04(1) (src:5712)
GIVEN `the person causes the other person to provide, or offer to provide, labour or a service` IS A BOOLEAN
      `by engaging in conduct that, in all the circumstances, could reasonably be expected to cause the other person to believe that their safety or the safety of a person known to them would be threatened if they failed to provide, or offer to provide, the labour or service` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 279.04(1) the person exploits another person` MEANS
    IF `the person causes the other person to provide, or offer to provide, labour or a service` AND `by engaging in conduct that, in all the circumstances, could reasonably be expected to cause the other person to believe that their safety or the safety of a person known to them would be threatened if they failed to provide, or offer to provide, the labour or service`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "a person exploits another person if they cause them to provide, or offer to provide, labour or a service by engaging in conduct that" (a failed "if": marginal reading (a))

DECLARE `s 279.04(2) the circumstance` IS ONE OF
    `s 279.04(2) the nature of the relationship between the accused and the complainant`
    `s 279.04(2)(a) the accused used, or threatened or attempted to use, force or another form of coercion`
    `s 279.04(2)(b) the accused used deception`
    `s 279.04(2)(c) the accused abused a position of trust, power or authority`
    `s 279.04(2)(d) the accused engaged in controlling or directive behaviour`
    `s 279.04(2)(e) the accused subjected the complainant to degrading or humiliating behaviour`
    `s 279.04(2)(e.1) the accused used, or threatened or attempted to use, violence against any animal known to the complainant`
    `s 279.04(2)(e.2) the accused damaged, or threatened or attempted to damage, the complainant’s property or the property of anyone known to the complainant`
    `s 279.04(2)(f) the accused exposed the complainant to behaviour referred to in paragraphs (a) to (e.2) directed at another person`
    `s 279.04(2)(g) the accused received an undue benefit in relation to the labour or service`
    `s 279.04(2)(h) the complainant is vulnerable`
    `s 279.04(2)(i) the accused manipulated the complainant by targeting their vulnerabilities`
    `s 279.04(2) another circumstance`

-- 279.04(2): the Court "must consider all the circumstances, including" the relationship and every listed fact "with respect to which there is evidence".
-- src:5713 | Circumstances
-- src:5714 | (2) In determining whether an accused exploits a complainant under subsection (1), the Court must consider all the circumstances, including the nature of the relationship between the accused and the complainant and all of the following facts with respect to which there is evidence:
-- src:5715 | (a) the accused used, or threatened or attempted to use, force or another form of coercion;
-- src:5716 | (b) the accused used deception;
-- src:5717 | (c) the accused abused a position of trust, power or authority;
-- src:5718 | (d) the accused engaged in controlling or directive behaviour, including with respect to finances, living conditions, appearance, communications with others, the labour or service provided or offered to be provided or the advertising of the labour or service or documents that establish or purport to establish the person’s identity or immigration status;
-- src:5719 | (e) the accused subjected the complainant to degrading or humiliating behaviour;
-- src:5720 | (e.1) the accused used, or threatened or attempted to use, violence against any animal known to the complainant;
-- src:5721 | (e.2) the accused damaged, or threatened or attempted to damage, the complainant’s property or the property of anyone known to the complainant;
-- src:5722 | (f) the accused exposed the complainant to behaviour referred to in paragraphs (a) to (e.2) directed at another person;
-- src:5723 | (g) the accused received an undue benefit in relation to the labour or service;
-- src:5724 | (h) the complainant is vulnerable, including because of age, mental or physical disability or personal circumstances such as the use of intoxicating substances, isolation, social or economic disadvantage, immigration status or any circumstance that has resulted or may result in victimization;
-- src:5725 | (i) the accused manipulated the complainant by targeting their vulnerabilities.
@ref s 279.04(2) (src:5713-5725)
GIVEN circumstance IS A `s 279.04(2) the circumstance`
      `there is evidence with respect to the fact` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 279.04(2) the Court must consider the circumstance` MEANS
    CONSIDER circumstance
    WHEN `s 279.04(2) the nature of the relationship between the accused and the complainant` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 279.04(2) another circumstance` THEN JUST TRUE   -- the lead-in: "all the circumstances"
    OTHERWISE
        IF `there is evidence with respect to the fact`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "all of the following facts with respect to which there is evidence"

-- src:5726 | Organ or tissue removal
-- src:5727 | (3) For the purposes of sections 279.01 to 279.03, a person exploits another person if they cause them, by means of deception or the use or threat of force or of any other form of coercion, to have an organ or tissue removed.
@ref s 279.04(3) (src:5726-5727)
GIVEN `the person causes the other person to have an organ or tissue removed` IS A BOOLEAN
      `by means of deception or the use or threat of force or of any other form of coercion` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 279.04(3) the person exploits another person` MEANS
    IF `the person causes the other person to have an organ or tissue removed` AND `by means of deception or the use or threat of force or of any other form of coercion`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "a person exploits another person if they cause them, by means of deception or the use or threat of force or of any other form of coercion, to have an organ or tissue removed" (a failed "if": marginal reading (a))

-- Subsections (1) and (3) are two sufficient routes, neither "only if": the composition is JUST TRUE by either, and otherwise NOTHING.
@ref s 279.04(1) and (3) (src:5726-5727)
GIVEN `the answer of s 279.04(1)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the answer of s 279.04(3)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 279.04 the person exploits another person for the purposes of sections 279.01 to 279.03` MEANS
    IF (`the answer of s 279.04(1)` EQUALS JUST TRUE) OR (`the answer of s 279.04(3)` EQUALS JUST TRUE)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): subsections (1) and (3) each say "exploits another person if" and neither says "only if"

DECLARE `s 279.04(4) the kind of safety` IS ONE OF
    `s 279.04(4) psychological safety`
    `s 279.04(4) safety of another kind`

-- src:5728 | For greater certainty
-- src:5729 | (4) For the purposes of this section, and for greater certainty, a person’s safety includes their psychological safety.
@ref s 279.04(4) (src:5728-5729)
GIVEN kind IS A `s 279.04(4) the kind of safety`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 279.04(4) a person’s safety includes this kind of safety` MEANS
    CONSIDER kind
    WHEN `s 279.04(4) psychological safety` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 279.04(4) safety of another kind` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "a person’s safety includes their psychological safety" does not say what else it includes

§ `s 279.1 -- Hostage taking`

-- src:5731 | 279.1 (1) Everyone takes a person hostage who — with intent to induce any person, other than the hostage, or any group of persons or any state or international or intergovernmental organization to commit or cause to be committed any act or omission as a condition, whether express or implied, of the release of the hostage —
-- src:5732 | (a) confines, imprisons, forcibly seizes or detains that person; and
-- src:5733 | (b) in any manner utters, conveys or causes any person to receive a threat that the death of, or bodily harm to, the hostage will be caused or that the confinement, imprisonment or detention of the hostage will be continued.
@ref s 279.1(1) (src:5731-5733)
GIVEN `the person acts with intent to induce any person, other than the hostage, or any group of persons or any state or international or intergovernmental organization to commit or cause to be committed any act or omission as a condition, whether express or implied, of the release of the hostage` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person confines, imprisons, forcibly seizes or detains that person` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person in any manner utters, conveys or causes any person to receive a threat that the death of, or bodily harm to, the hostage will be caused or that the confinement, imprisonment or detention of the hostage will be continued` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 279.1(1) the person takes a person hostage` MEANS
    IF `the person acts with intent to induce any person, other than the hostage, or any group of persons or any state or international or intergovernmental organization to commit or cause to be committed any act or omission as a condition, whether express or implied, of the release of the hostage`
       AND `the person confines, imprisons, forcibly seizes or detains that person`
       AND `the person in any manner utters, conveys or causes any person to receive a threat that the death of, or bodily harm to, the hostage will be caused or that the confinement, imprisonment or detention of the hostage will be continued`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Everyone takes a person hostage who"

-- 279.1(2): the punishment, with the same limbs as 279(1.1)(a), (a.1) and (b) (no limb for the age of the victim).
-- src:5734 | Hostage-taking
-- src:5735 | (2) Every person who takes a person hostage is guilty of an indictable offence and liable
-- src:5736 | (a) if a restricted firearm or prohibited firearm is used in the commission of the offence or if any firearm is used in the commission of the offence and the offence is committed for the benefit of, at the direction of, or in association with, a criminal organization, to imprisonment for life and to a minimum punishment of imprisonment for a term of
-- src:5737 | (i) in the case of a first offence, five years, and
-- src:5738 | (ii) in the case of a second or subsequent offence, seven years;
-- src:5739 | (a.1) in any other case where a firearm is used in the commission of the offence, to imprisonment for life and to a minimum punishment of imprisonment for a term of four years; and
-- src:5740 | (b) in any other case, to imprisonment for life.
@ref s 279.1(2) (src:5734-5740)
GIVEN `s 2.1 restricted firearm: a restricted firearm is used in the commission of the offence` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `s 2.1 prohibited firearm: a prohibited firearm is used in the commission of the offence` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `s 2 firearm: a firearm is used in the commission of the offence` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `s 2 criminal organization: the offence is committed for the benefit of, at the direction of, or in association with, a criminal organization` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the answer of s 279.1(2.1) as to a second or subsequent offence` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE Punishment
`s 279.1(2) the punishment` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF    (`s 2.1 restricted firearm: a restricted firearm is used in the commission of the offence` EQUALS NOTHING)
           OR (`s 2.1 prohibited firearm: a prohibited firearm is used in the commission of the offence` EQUALS NOTHING)
           OR (`s 2 firearm: a firearm is used in the commission of the offence` EQUALS NOTHING)
           OR (`s 2 criminal organization: the offence is committed for the benefit of, at the direction of, or in association with, a criminal organization` EQUALS NOTHING)
        THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): which firearm, and whether a criminal organization is involved, are for s 2, s 2.1 and s 84(1) and s 467.1(1), and are not determined
        IF `paragraph (a) applies` AND (`the answer of s 279.1(2.1) as to a second or subsequent offence` EQUALS NOTHING)
        THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether this is a second or subsequent offence is for s 279.1(2.1) and is not determined
        OTHERWISE JUST (Punishment OF `by indictment`, `imprisonment for life`, `the minimum imprisonment`, `no fine is stated`, `no fine is stated`)
    WHERE
        `paragraph (a) applies` MEANS
                (`s 2.1 restricted firearm: a restricted firearm is used in the commission of the offence` EQUALS JUST TRUE)
             OR (`s 2.1 prohibited firearm: a prohibited firearm is used in the commission of the offence` EQUALS JUST TRUE)
             OR ((`s 2 firearm: a firearm is used in the commission of the offence` EQUALS JUST TRUE) AND (`s 2 criminal organization: the offence is committed for the benefit of, at the direction of, or in association with, a criminal organization` EQUALS JUST TRUE))
        `paragraph (a.1) applies` MEANS (`s 2 firearm: a firearm is used in the commission of the offence` EQUALS JUST TRUE) AND (NOT `paragraph (a) applies`)
        `the minimum in years` MEANS
            BRANCH
                IF `paragraph (a) applies` AND (`the answer of s 279.1(2.1) as to a second or subsequent offence` EQUALS JUST TRUE) THEN 7
                IF `paragraph (a) applies` THEN 5
                IF `paragraph (a.1) applies` THEN 4
                OTHERWISE 0
        `the minimum imprisonment` MEANS
            IF `the minimum in years` EQUALS 0 THEN `no imprisonment is stated` ELSE `imprisonment for a term of` (`Length of time` OF `the minimum in years`, 0, 0, FALSE)

@ref s 279.1(2) (src:5734-5735)
`s 279.1(2) the class of the offence` MEANS `an indictable offence`

-- src:5741 | Subsequent offences
-- src:5742 | (2.1) In determining, for the purpose of paragraph (2)(a), whether a convicted person has committed a second or subsequent offence, if the person was earlier convicted of any of the following offences, that offence is to be considered as an earlier offence:
-- src:5743 | (a) an offence under this section;
-- src:5744 | (b) an offence under subsection 85(1) or (2) or section 244 or 244.2; or
-- src:5745 | (c) an offence under section 220, 236, 239, 272 or 273, subsection 279(1) or section 344 or 346 if a firearm was used in the commission of the offence.
-- src:5746 | However, an earlier offence shall not be taken into account if 10 years have elapsed between the day on which the person was convicted of the earlier offence and the day on which the person was convicted of the offence for which sentence is being imposed, not taking into account any time in custody.
@ref s 279.1(2.1) (src:5741-5746)
DECLARE `s 279.1(2.1) earlier conviction` HAS
    `the offence of which the person was convicted`                     IS A `Provision of the Code`
    `a firearm was used in the commission of that offence`              IS A BOOLEAN
    `the day on which the person was convicted of that offence`         IS A DATE
    `the days in custody between the two convictions`                   IS A NUMBER

@ref s 279.1(2.1) (src:5741-5746)
GIVEN conviction IS A `s 279.1(2.1) earlier conviction`
      `the day on which the person was convicted of the offence for which sentence is being imposed` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 279.1(2.1) the conviction is to be considered as an earlier offence` MEANS
    IF NOT `the conviction is of an offence the subsection lists`
    THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "if the person was earlier convicted of any of the following offences, that offence is to be considered as an earlier offence"
    ELSE IF `ten years have elapsed`
         THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "an earlier offence shall not be taken into account if 10 years have elapsed between the day on which the person was convicted of the earlier offence and the day on which the person was convicted of the offence for which sentence is being imposed, not taking into account any time in custody"
         ELSE JUST TRUE
    WHERE
        sec MEANS conviction's `the offence of which the person was convicted`'s `section`
        sub MEANS conviction's `the offence of which the person was convicted`'s `subsection`
        `the conviction is of an offence the subsection lists` MEANS
                sec EQUALS 279.1
             OR (sec EQUALS 85 AND (sub EQUALS "(1)" OR sub EQUALS "(2)"))
             OR sec EQUALS 244 OR sec EQUALS 244.2
             OR (   (sec EQUALS 220 OR sec EQUALS 236 OR sec EQUALS 239 OR sec EQUALS 272 OR sec EQUALS 273 OR (sec EQUALS 279 AND sub EQUALS "(1)") OR sec EQUALS 344 OR sec EQUALS 346)
                AND conviction's `a firearm was used in the commission of that offence`)
        `the anniversary ten years after the earlier conviction` MEANS
            Date (DATE_DAY (conviction's `the day on which the person was convicted of that offence`)) (DATE_MONTH (conviction's `the day on which the person was convicted of that offence`)) ((DATE_YEAR (conviction's `the day on which the person was convicted of that offence`)) PLUS 10)
        `ten years have elapsed` MEANS
            ((DATE_SERIAL `the day on which the person was convicted of the offence for which sentence is being imposed`) MINUS conviction's `the days in custody between the two convictions`) AT LEAST (DATE_SERIAL `the anniversary ten years after the earlier conviction`)

-- src:5747 | Sequence of convictions only
-- src:5748 | (2.2) For the purposes of subsection (2.1), the only question to be considered is the sequence of convictions and no consideration shall be given to the sequence of commission of offences or whether any offence occurred before or after any conviction.
@ref s 279.1(2.2) (src:5747-5748)
GIVEN `the day on which the person was convicted of the earlier offence` IS A DATE
      `the day on which the person was convicted of the offence for which sentence is being imposed` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 279.1(2.2) the conviction is earlier in the sequence of convictions` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF (DATE_SERIAL `the day on which the person was convicted of the earlier offence`) LESS THAN (DATE_SERIAL `the day on which the person was convicted of the offence for which sentence is being imposed`) THEN JUST TRUE
        IF (DATE_SERIAL `the day on which the person was convicted of the earlier offence`) GREATER THAN (DATE_SERIAL `the day on which the person was convicted of the offence for which sentence is being imposed`) THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the only question to be considered is the sequence of convictions" (a conviction that follows in the sequence is not an earlier one)
        OTHERWISE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the text does not say how two convictions on the same day are sequenced

@ref s 279.1(2.1) and (2.2) (src:5747-5748)
GIVEN `the earlier convictions` IS A LIST OF `s 279.1(2.1) earlier conviction`
      `the day on which the person was convicted of the offence for which sentence is being imposed` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 279.1(2.1) the person has committed a second or subsequent offence` MEANS
    IF any (GIVEN c IS A `s 279.1(2.1) earlier conviction` YIELD (`the conviction counts` c) EQUALS JUST TRUE) `the earlier convictions`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE IF any (GIVEN c IS A `s 279.1(2.1) earlier conviction` YIELD (`the conviction counts` c) EQUALS NOTHING) `the earlier convictions`
         THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): an earlier conviction of an offence the subsection does not list, or on the same day, is not said to count or not to count
         ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "in the case of a first offence" (no earlier conviction counts: none, or each is barred by ten years)
    WHERE
        `the conviction counts` c MEANS
            BRANCH
                IF (`s 279.1(2.2) the conviction is earlier in the sequence of convictions` (c's `the day on which the person was convicted of that offence`) `the day on which the person was convicted of the offence for which sentence is being imposed`) EQUALS JUST FALSE THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the only question to be considered is the sequence of convictions"
                IF (`s 279.1(2.2) the conviction is earlier in the sequence of convictions` (c's `the day on which the person was convicted of that offence`) `the day on which the person was convicted of the offence for which sentence is being imposed`) EQUALS NOTHING THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): two convictions on one day
                OTHERWISE `s 279.1(2.1) the conviction is to be considered as an earlier offence` c `the day on which the person was convicted of the offence for which sentence is being imposed`

-- src:5749 | (3) [Repealed, 2018, c. 29, s. 27]
@ref s 279.1(3) (src:5749)
`s 279.1(3) as the text shows it` MEANS "[Repealed, 2018, c. 29, s. 27]"


§ `ss 280 to 283 -- Abduction`

-- src:5751 | 280 (1) Every person who, without lawful authority, takes or causes to be taken a person under the age of 16 years out of the possession of and against the will of the parent or guardian of that person or of any other person who has the lawful care or charge of that person is guilty of
-- src:5752 | (a) an indictable offence and liable to imprisonment for a term of not more than five years; or
-- src:5753 | (b) an offence punishable on summary conviction.
@ref s 280(1) (src:5751-5753)
GIVEN `the person acts without lawful authority` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person takes or causes to be taken a person under the age of 16 years` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person does so out of the possession of and against the will of the parent or guardian of that person or of any other person who has the lawful care or charge of that person` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 280(1) the person is guilty of the offence of abduction of a person under age 16` MEANS
    IF `the person acts without lawful authority` AND `the person takes or causes to be taken a person under the age of 16 years` AND `the person does so out of the possession of and against the will of the parent or guardian of that person or of any other person who has the lawful care or charge of that person`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "without lawful authority, takes or causes to be taken a person under the age of 16 years out of the possession of and against the will of the parent or guardian"

@ref s 280(1) (src:5751-5753)
`s 280(1) the class of the offence` MEANS `an offence that the section makes both indictable and punishable on summary conviction`

@ref s 280(1) (src:5752-5753)
GIVEN mode IS A `Mode of proceeding`
      `s 787(1) the general penalty for an offence punishable on summary conviction` IS A Punishment
GIVETH A Punishment
`s 280(1) the punishment` MEANS
    CONSIDER mode
    WHEN `by indictment` THEN Punishment OF `by indictment`, (`imprisonment for a term of` `five years`), `no imprisonment is stated`, `no fine is stated`, `no fine is stated`
    WHEN `on summary conviction` THEN `s 787(1) the general penalty for an offence punishable on summary conviction`

