      `the person unlawfully takes, entices away, conceals, detains, receives or harbours that person` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person does so with intent to deprive a parent or guardian, or any other person who has the lawful care or charge of that person, of the possession of that person` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 281 the person is guilty of the offence of abduction of a person under age 14` MEANS
    IF `the person is not the parent, guardian or person having the lawful care or charge of a person under the age of 14 years` AND `the person unlawfully takes, entices away, conceals, detains, receives or harbours that person` AND `the person does so with intent to deprive a parent or guardian, or any other person who has the lawful care or charge of that person, of the possession of that person`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "not being the parent, guardian or person having the lawful care or charge of a person under the age of 14 years, unlawfully takes, entices away, conceals, detains, receives or harbours that person with intent to deprive"

@ref s 281 (src:5757-5759)
`s 281 the class of the offence` MEANS `an offence that the section makes both indictable and punishable on summary conviction`

