-- 283(2): a bar. "without the consent": with consent the bar is lifted and the text says nothing further (NOTHING).
-- src:5770 | Consent required
-- src:5771 | (2) No proceedings may be commenced under subsection (1) without the consent of the Attorney General or counsel instructed by him for that purpose.
@ref s 283(2) (src:5770-5771)
GIVEN `the consent of the Attorney General or counsel instructed by him for that purpose has been given` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 283(2) proceedings under subsection (1) may not be commenced` MEANS
    IF NOT `the consent of the Attorney General or counsel instructed by him for that purpose has been given`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "No proceedings may be commenced under subsection (1) without the consent of the Attorney General or counsel instructed by him for that purpose" (with consent the bar does not apply and the section says nothing more)

§ `ss 284 to 286 -- Defences and no defence`

-- 284: a defence. Made out: JUST TRUE; not made out by an offence under ss 281 to 283: "this section gives no defence on these facts" (JUST FALSE).
-- src:5773 | 284 No one shall be found guilty of an offence under sections 281 to 283 if he establishes that the taking, enticing away, concealing, detaining, receiving or harbouring of any young person was done with the consent of the parent, guardian or other person having the lawful possession, care or charge of that young person.
@ref s 284 (src:5773)
GIVEN offence IS A `Provision of the Code`
      `the person charged establishes that the taking, enticing away, concealing, detaining, receiving or harbouring of the young person was done with the consent of the parent, guardian or other person having the lawful possession, care or charge of that young person` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 284 the consent of the parent, guardian or other person having lawful possession bars a finding of guilt` MEANS
    IF NOT (offence's `section` AT LEAST 281 AND offence's `section` AT MOST 283)
    THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "an offence under sections 281 to 283"
    ELSE IF `the person charged establishes that the taking, enticing away, concealing, detaining, receiving or harbouring of the young person was done with the consent of the parent, guardian or other person having the lawful possession, care or charge of that young person`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "if he establishes that the taking, enticing away, concealing, detaining, receiving or harbouring of any young person was done with the consent of the parent, guardian or other person having the lawful possession, care or charge of that young person" (this section gives no defence on these facts)

-- src:5775 | 285 No one shall be found guilty of an offence under sections 280 to 283 if the court is satisfied that the taking, enticing away, concealing, detaining, receiving or harbouring of any young person was necessary to protect the young person from danger of imminent harm or if the person charged with the offence was escaping from danger of imminent harm.
@ref s 285 (src:5775)
GIVEN offence IS A `Provision of the Code`
      `the court is satisfied that the taking, enticing away, concealing, detaining, receiving or harbouring of the young person was necessary to protect the young person from danger of imminent harm` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person charged with the offence was escaping from danger of imminent harm` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 285 the danger of imminent harm bars a finding of guilt` MEANS
    IF NOT (offence's `section` AT LEAST 280 AND offence's `section` AT MOST 283)
    THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "an offence under sections 280 to 283"
    ELSE IF `the court is satisfied that the taking, enticing away, concealing, detaining, receiving or harbouring of the young person was necessary to protect the young person from danger of imminent harm` OR `the person charged with the offence was escaping from danger of imminent harm`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "if the court is satisfied that the taking, enticing away, concealing, detaining, receiving or harbouring of any young person was necessary to protect the young person from danger of imminent harm or if the person charged with the offence was escaping from danger of imminent harm" (this section gives no defence on these facts)

-- The offence of s 280 after the defence of s 285, and of ss 281 to 283 after ss 284 and 285: a defence that applies is the text's no ("No one shall be found guilty").
@ref s 280 composed with s 285 (src:5775)
GIVEN `the answer of the offence function` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the answer of s 285` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 280 and s 285 the person is guilty of the offence of abduction of a person under age 16 after the defence` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the answer of s 285` EQUALS JUST TRUE THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "No one shall be found guilty of an offence under sections 280 to 283 if the court is satisfied"
        IF (`the answer of the offence function` EQUALS JUST TRUE) AND (`the answer of s 285` EQUALS JUST FALSE) THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): the offence or the defence is not covered

-- src:5773 | 284 No one shall be found guilty of an offence under sections 281 to 283 if he establishes that the taking, enticing away, concealing, detaining, receiving or harbouring of any young person was done with the consent of the parent, guardian or other person having the lawful possession, care or charge of that young person.
