      `the answer of s 284` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the answer of s 285` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 281 to 283 and ss 284 and 285 the person is guilty of the offence after the defences` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF (`the answer of s 284` EQUALS JUST TRUE) OR (`the answer of s 285` EQUALS JUST TRUE) THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "No one shall be found guilty of an offence under sections 281 to 283 if he establishes"
        IF (`the answer of the offence function` EQUALS JUST TRUE) AND (`the answer of s 284` EQUALS JUST FALSE) AND (`the answer of s 285` EQUALS JUST FALSE) THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): the offence or a defence is not covered

-- src:5777 | 286 In proceedings in respect of an offence under sections 280 to 283, it is not a defence to any charge that a young person consented to or suggested any conduct of the accused.
@ref s 286 (src:5777)
GIVEN offence IS A `Provision of the Code`
      `the young person consented to or suggested conduct of the accused` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 286 the young person’s consent or suggestion is a defence` MEANS
    IF offence's `section` AT LEAST 280 AND offence's `section` AT MOST 283 AND `the young person consented to or suggested conduct of the accused`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "it is not a defence to any charge that a young person consented to or suggested any conduct of the accused"
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "In proceedings in respect of an offence under sections 280 to 283, it is not a defence to any charge that a young person consented to or suggested any conduct"
